tead to make sure it gets linked when needed.  This will fix arc-cros-gralloc without breaking other packages.  BUG=b:65189615 TEST=rebuilt arc-llvm, arc-mesa, arc-cros-gralloc, and      arc-amdgpu-addrlib  Change-Id: Ifbcf4714b413ecd6f8eeb91c4487c4f4839b1f26 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/905241 Commit-Ready: Benjamin Gordon &lt;bmgordon@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Benjamin Gordon &lt;bmgordon@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Tomasz Figa &lt;tfiga@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="905241" owner_email="bmgordon@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/41/905241/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master-0.3.13" change_id="I44dc1b27e27ca14f1bb6906f90e74c19fa0ddde8" commit="7a11117560b9ec1ca56269e7c371d4457bd33d12" commit_message="Trousers: Fix memory leaks in Tspi_TPM_ActivateIdentity  Fix resource cleanup on error handling paths in Tspi_TPM_ActivateIdentity(). Leaking were |cb|, |symKeyBlob|, |symCAAttestation.algorithm.parms| and |symCAAttestation.credential| (each under slightly different conditions).  BUG=chromium:808001 TEST=none (relying on existing tests)  Change-Id: I44dc1b27e27ca14f1bb6906f90e74c19fa0ddde8 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/897614 Commit-Ready: Maksim Ivanov &lt;emaxx@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Maksim Ivanov &lt;emaxx@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Andrey Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="897614" owner_email="emaxx@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/third_party/trousers" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/trousers" ref="refs/changes/14/897614/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5dd4fe37df8dbd1b34bdc40e2e42a64e96b4233c" commit="ac62a757243949c7b6466eba27901ee02406de7f" commit_message="cryptohome: Add protobuf for hash tree leaf data  Instead of writing a raw vector, encapsulate the leaf data into a protobuf before writing it out to the disk.  Also, modify the logic of GenerateAndStoreHashCache(), so that all the leaf nodes are first updated in the HashCache file, and then CalculateHash() generates all the inner hashes.  Additonally, slightly change the semantics of GetLabelData(); now, if the label doesn't exist in the tree, return an all-zero HMAC. Return false only if we aren't able to read the leaf label value due to an error.  Also, change the return types of PersistentLookupTable functions to disambiguate between table storage errors, and keys not being present.  Finally, remove some unused code in the unit tests.  BUG=chromium:794010, chromium:809703 TEST=cryptohome unit tests pass  Change-Id: I5dd4fe37df8dbd1b34bdc40e2e42a64e96b4233c Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/902612 Commit-Ready: Prashant Malani &lt;pmalani@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Prashant Malani &lt;pmalani@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Prashant Malani &lt;pmalani@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="902612" owner_email="pmalani@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/12/902612/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia395d65eb1ea3e96060e5de31f190b3c14f42595" commit="c96c8f4a832091be6e01043b51a377262c39b8d1" commit_message="rockchip: support user ae controls.  Parse the user AE control settings and pass the parameters to 3A library.  BUG=b:69276988 TEST=Build on scarlet  Change-Id: Ia395d65eb1ea3e96060e5de31f190b3c14f42595 Signed-off-by: ZhongYiChong &lt;zyc@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/844404 Commit-Ready: Jeffy Chen &lt;jeffy.chen@rock-chips.com&g